# org-target: docs/10-19-design/10-architecture/10.08-engineering-library-and-rust-trajectories.org::#rust-evidence-trajectories
direction: down
classes: {
  input: {style: {fill: "#EAF2FF"; stroke: "#315B8A"; border-radius: 10; font-size: 17}}
  state: {style: {fill: "#E6F5F3"; stroke: "#19756C"; border-radius: 10; font-size: 17}}
  gate: {style: {fill: "#FFF2DD"; stroke: "#9B6C25"; border-radius: 10; font-size: 17}}
}
shared: "Shared engineering Library / Catalog\nRust ownership / layout / async / parallelism\nContributors maintain domain rules and factors\nDesign patterns / Scenarios / counterexamples\nEvidence templates and reusable trajectories\nExisting POO Module / Profile / Scenario" {class: input}
context: "Applying project's actual context\nIndexing / compression / batch / gateway\nWorkload / hardware / runtime / source / tenant\nLLM-based AI agent hypotheses and candidate architectures\nExact claim interpretation and method scope\nSource-project receipt is not target-project proof" {class: input}
reason: "ASCENT Scheme / Datalog + Evidence DSL\nEvaluate represented support / counter / conflict\nDerive domain obligations and missing premises\nReassess changed current dependencies\nRules do not manufacture external truth" {class: state}
performance: "RT-P performance and resource trajectory\nBounded queue -> whole-memory obligations\nWaiting producers may refute total-memory claim\nRevised admission / cancellation design\nActual matched throughput / p99 / CPU / RSS evidence" {class: gate}
security: "RT-S cache / safety trajectory\nThroughput candidate -> tenant and hit policy\nRevocation-at-hit / resource counter Scenarios\nQNT model + source mapping + actual authority\nNo old-grant reuse by cache-key coincidence" {class: gate}
concurrency: "RT-C shared-state / atomic trajectory\nLock replacement is a design hypothesis\nInvariant / ordering / reclamation obligations\nLean or QNT scoped result plus native correspondence\nActual contention measurement still required" {class: gate}
review: "Actual evidence and reviewed Library contribution\nTools / models / proofs / measurements / counterresults\nIndependent oracle, source and applicability checks\nRetain failures and unresolved work\nFeedback supports the LLM-based AI agent's next alternative investigation" {class: input}
shared -> context -> reason
reason -> performance
reason -> security
reason -> concurrency
performance -> review
security -> review
concurrency -> review
review -> shared: "reviewed reusable knowledge, not universal acceptance"
review -> context: "new project-bound evidence and alternatives"
